{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 23,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou sittest to eat with a ruler, consider diligently what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And put a knife to thy throat, if thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man given to appetite.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not desirous of his dainties: for they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " deceitful food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Labor not to be rich: cease from thy own wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou set thy eyes upon that which is not? for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "riches",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " certainly make to themselves wings; they fly away as an eagle towards heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Eat thou not the bread of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an evil eye, neither desire thou his dainties:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For as he thinketh in his heart, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he: Eat and drink, saith he to thee; but his heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The morsel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast eaten shalt thou vomit up, and lose thy sweet words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Speak not in the ears of a fool: for he will despise the wisdom of thy words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remove not the old landmark; and enter not into the fields of the fatherless:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For their redeemer ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty; he will plead their cause with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Apply thy heart to instruction, and thy ears to the words of knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Withhold not correction from the child: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou beatest him with the rod, he shall not die.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt beat him with the rod, and shalt deliver his soul from hell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, if thy heart be wise, my heart shall rejoice, even mine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, my reins shall rejoice, when thy lips speak right things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not thy heart envy sinners: but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the fear of the LORD all the day long.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For surely there is an end; and thy expectation shall not be cut off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear thou, my son, and be wise, and guide thy heart in the way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not among wine-bibbers; among riotous eaters of flesh:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the drunkard and the glutton shall come to poverty: and drowsiness shall clothe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with rags.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken to thy father that begat thee, and despise not thy mother when she is old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Buy the truth, and sell ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "also",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The father of the righteous shall greatly rejoice: and he that begetteth a wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "child",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall have joy of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy father and thy mother shall be glad, and she that bore thee shall rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, give me thy heart, and let thy eyes observe my ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a lewd woman ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a deep ditch; and a strange woman ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a narrow pit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She also lieth in wait as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a prey, and increaseth the transgressors among men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath woe? who hath sorrow? who hath contentions? who hath babbling? who hath wounds without cause? who hath redness of eyes?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that tarry long at the wine; they that go to seek mixed wine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look not thou upon the wine when it is red, when it giveth its color in the cup, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it moveth itself aright.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At the last it biteth like a serpent, and stingeth like an adder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy eyes shall behold strange women, and thy heart shall utter perverse things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt be as he that lieth down in the midst of the sea, or as he that lieth upon the top of a mast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.23.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have stricken me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wilt thou say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I was not sick; they have beaten me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I felt ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not: when shall I awake? I will seek it yet again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
